  "comparison_table": "| Graph | Measured rate | Earlier shuffle medians and Holm p | N-STRENGTH median and Holm p | Verdict |\n|---|---:|---|---|---|\n| T1a | 2.65 Hz | N-FULL 113.67 Hz (Holm p 0.008); N-CONTEXT 110.73 Hz (Holm p 0.008); N-SIGN 119.78 Hz (Holm p 0.008) | N-STRENGTH 4.40 Hz (Holm p 0.088) | The stricter control removes most of the rate gap; its comparison is not significant. |\n| Full MaleCNS | 15.31 Hz | N-SIGN 36.84 Hz (Holm p 0.04) | N-STRENGTH 14.48 Hz (Holm p 0.14) | No significant rate difference from the stricter control. |\n| T2 | 10.00 Hz | N-FULL 72.08 Hz (Holm p 0.02); N-SIGN 29.66 Hz (Holm p 0.02) | N-STRENGTH 4.99 Hz (Holm p 0.02) | Measured wiring is faster than N-STRENGTH, the opposite direction. |",
  "dataset_doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23409752",
  "exploratory": [
    "EXPLORATORY E1: measured leading signed eigenvalues are 3.04103 for T1a and 6.91182 for T2, above every family median; 2 null eigenvalues did not converge and remain missing. Structure and Spearman associations are descriptive, not a causal mechanism test.",
    "EXPLORATORY E2a (glutamate treated as excitatory): measured rate 139.557 Hz versus null median 264.911 Hz; measured critical coupling 0.015 versus null median 0.01. Measured rate percentile 0%; critical-coupling percentile 100%. Both measured and shuffled wiring saturate under this sign assumption.",
    "EXPLORATORY E3-low (lower noise): measured rate 1.52497 Hz versus null median 116.096 Hz; measured critical coupling >0.1 (censored) versus null median 0.03. Measured rate percentile 0%; critical-coupling percentile 100%.",
    "EXPLORATORY E3-high (higher noise): measured rate 4.13383 Hz versus null median 119.603 Hz; measured critical coupling >0.1 (censored) versus null median 0.03. Measured rate percentile 0%; critical-coupling percentile 100%.",
    "EXPLORATORY E2b: preregistered SKIPPED. Compiled predicted_nt_confidence is copied verbatim, but the source confidence semantics and its relationship to consensus_nt signs are not established. No threshold interpretation is invented."
  ],
  "families": [
    "H0-STR (T1a), N-STRENGTH: the registered stability result did not replicate. H0a: measured >0.1 (censored) versus null median 0.1, Holm p 0.088, not significant; does not establish the stability difference; H0b: measured 2.65068 versus null median 4.40042, Holm p 0.088, not significant; does not establish the stability difference.",
    "H0-FULL (FULL), N-SIGN: the stability difference holds under this model. H0b-FULL: measured 15.3095 versus null median 36.8414, Holm p 0.04, supports the registered stability direction.",
    "H0-FULL (FULL), N-STRENGTH: the registered stability result did not replicate. H0b-FULL: measured 15.3095 versus null median 14.4829, Holm p 0.14, not significant; does not establish the stability difference.",
    "H0-T2 (T2), N-FULL: the stability difference holds under this model. H0a: measured >0.1 (censored) versus null median 0.039, Holm p 0.02, supports the registered stability direction; H0b: measured 10.0006 versus null median 72.0766, Holm p 0.02, supports the registered stability direction.",
    "H0-T2 (T2), N-SIGN: the stability difference holds under this model. H0a: measured >0.1 (censored) versus null median 0.05, Holm p 0.02, supports the registered stability direction; H0b: measured 10.0006 versus null median 29.658, Holm p 0.02, supports the registered stability direction.",
    "H0-T2 (T2), N-STRENGTH: the registered stability result did not replicate. H0a: measured >0.1 (censored) versus null median >0.1 (censored), Holm p 1, not significant; does not establish the stability difference; H0b: measured 10.0006 versus null median 4.98657, Holm p 0.02, opposite direction: measured rate is higher."
  ],
  "game_disclosure": "Game v2.9 has two hands: a press shorter than 300 ms uses the existing flick (speed 0.04, radius 0.8); a press of 300 ms or longer uses the existing swat (speed 0.025, radius 1.4). Flight lasts 330 ms at 0.018 arena units/ms, a 5.94-unit path. The first 120 ms, direction jitter and wall reflection stay as in v2.8.",
  "game_profile_id": "flybench.game.v2.9",
  "lab_caveat": "This shuffle keeps each neuron's excitatory and inhibitory partner counts and signs, but not its total input strength. Shuffles that also approximately keep input strength stay almost as calm as measured wiring: in the registered T1a comparison at coupling 0.039, measured wiring averaged 2.65 Hz, N-SIGN 119.78 Hz and N-STRENGTH 4.40 Hz (N-STRENGTH Holm p 0.088).",
  "lab_drive_disclosure": "Lab simulations have no walking drive.",
  "lab_heading": "Measured vs shuffled wiring",
  "lab_seeds": {
    "environment": 8128,
    "neural": 2027101401
  },
  "limitations": "These results apply only to this simplified model, with no claims about living flies. A non-significant result does not establish equivalence. Escape and walking comparisons remain insufficient.",
  "mechanism": "EXPLORATORY: the earlier shuffles flattened the input-strength distribution in T1a (Gini about 0.47, versus 0.65 measured), while N-STRENGTH kept it close (about 0.64). This suggests that, in this model, stability mainly reflects how unevenly input strength is spread across neurons rather than which partners connect. This explanation was not a preregistered mechanism test; the E1 descriptors were preregistered as exploratory.",
  "original": "In this model, measured wiring stays calm at couplings where shuffles that keep each neuron's partner counts and signs saturate.",
